id=a52sxq_kernel_bone_machine
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: bone-machine kernel 5.4.302
author=kusti420
description=Replaces the stock A528BXXU5FWK4 kernel (Linux 5.4.233, Nov 2023) with bone-machine's One UI kernel, Linux 5.4.302-bone-machine-qgki (final 5.4 LTS sublevel), built 2026-10-08 from source (https://github.com/mna08072-cmyk/android_kernel_samsung_sm7325_a52s_5g branch resukisu-oneui @93b49d0ccd89, ReSukiSU 35203; upstream bone-machine/android_kernel_samsung_sm7325_a52s_5g) plus k4 patches (CAP_PERFMON/CAP_BPF/CAP_CHECKPOINT_RESTORE, GPU NAP and stock GPU voltage/315 MHz init level restored, KGSL idle timeout 80 ms, BTF for Android 17's BPF CPU-time tracking: CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF with 5.4-compatible pahole kinds, BPF_MAP_TYPE_RINGBUF backport for Google's Tethering APEX, KernelSU stat hook on native newfstatat/statx so su works). Artifact prebuilts/kernel/bone-machine/bone-machine_k4btf_ringbuf_su_a52sxq.zip, sha256 885b9b082e747d3470ea6eaed25c6781edadb3d3e3b26134afa2d627951caee2 (see SOURCE.txt). Swaps only the kernel Image inside our boot.img (our ramdisk, cmdline and 2023-11 OS patch level stay), and uses the release's vendor_boot.img (same first-stage fstab, its 84 modules rebuilt for this kernel incl. wlan.ko, matching dtb) and dtbo.img. NOTE: the kernel has ReSukiSU (KernelSU fork) built in (dormant without its manager app) and Samsung Knox/RKP/KDP/DEFEX/PROCA/FIVE/DSMS disabled.
